.TH TULPAR-INFO 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.2.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-info, tulpar-show \- show full metadata for a package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar info
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar show
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar n
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-n
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows full metadata for
.IR name .
The local package database is checked first; if the package is not
installed, the configured repositories are queried instead.
.B info
and
.B show
are equivalent spellings of the same command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Look up in the local database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the metadata as a JSON object instead of human-readable text.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the package was found, non-zero otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-search (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1)
